Q] What is a Stream ?
Ans :-
  - Java Provides new additional package in java 8 called java.util.stream.
  - stream API perform bulk operation and process objects of collection
  - Main Advantage of stream is to reduce the length of code.


* Various Core Operations Over Streams :

✅ Intermediate Operations  :-

 Intermediate operations are operations that transform a stream into another stream.
 These operations don’t produce a result immediately — instead, they build a pipeline of operations that are executed only when a terminal operation is invoked.



Key Characteristics:
Return Type: Always return a new Stream.

Lazy Evaluation: They are lazy — no processing occurs until a terminal operation is called.

Chainable: Multiple intermediate operations can be chained together to form complex data processing pipelines.



🔍 Filtering
Method	                             Description
filter(Predicate<T> predicate)	     Filters elements based on a condition.

distinct()	                         Removes duplicate elements (based on equals).

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


🔄 Mapping (Transformation)
Method	                                   Description
map(Function<T, R> mapper)	                        Transforms each element into another using a function.

mapToInt(ToIntFunction<T> mapper)	                Maps elements to an IntStream.

mapToLong(ToLongFunction<T>mapper)	                Maps elements to a LongStream.

mapToDouble(ToDoubleFunction<T> mapper)	            Maps elements to a DoubleStream.

flatMap(Function<T, Stream<R>> mapper)	            Flattens nested streams.

flatMapToInt(Function<T, IntStream> mapper)	        Flattens to IntStream.

flatMapToLong(Function<T, LongStream> mapper)	    Flattens to LongStream.

flatMapToDouble(Function<T, DoubleStream> mapper)	Flattens to DoubleStream.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

📐 Sorting
Method	                                 Description
sorted()	                             Sorts elements in natural order.

sorted(Comparator<T> comparator)	     Sorts using a custom comparator.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧪 Peeking

Method	                       Description
peek(Consumer<T> action)	   Performs an action on each element (usually for debugging).


------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🎯 Type Conversion (for primitives)

Method	                        Description
boxed()                        	Converts a primitive stream (IntStream, etc.) to an object stream.
asLongStream()	                Converts IntStream to LongStream (available on IntStream).
asDoubleStream()	            Converts IntStream to DoubleStream (available on IntStream).


